<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:10:50 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>Foiled Hindu temple plot exposes rising anti-Indian sentiment in the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261030-foiled-hindu-temple-plot-exposes-rising-anti-indian-sentiment-in-the-us</link><description>
In this edition of Access Asia, we explore why anti-Indian sentiment is rising in the United States in the wake of the foiled plot targeting a Hindu temple in Illinois. We ask the executive director of the Center for the Study of Organized Hate what's behind the trend, and whether the rhetoric coming from the Trump White House is to blame.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c141a4ba-d3b3-11f1-ba9c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-ind%C3%A9pendance-indienne.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c141a4ba-d3b3-11f1-ba9c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-ind%C3%A9pendance-indienne.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c50d131c-d38c-11f1-ad2e-6b9c3c15f12d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:02:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Delano D’SOUZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>North Korea tests attack drones as Kim calls for 'absolute superiority'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261030-north-korea-tests-attack-drones-as-kim-calls-for-absolute-superiority</link><description>
North Korea has tested attack drones, cruise missiles and rocket launchers at a weapons demonstration, state media reported Friday, as Kim Jong Un called for faster development of military drone and artificial intelligence technology. The tests follow a series of weapons trials and rising tensions with South Korea.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f840fcc-d3f3-11f1-bc65-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-29T230502Z-1125020976-RC29DOAMMSDH-RTRMADP-3-NORTHKOREA-ARMS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f840fcc-d3f3-11f1-bc65-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-29T230502Z-1125020976-RC29DOAMMSDH-RTRMADP-3-NORTHKOREA-ARMS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e252b5a-d3f8-11f1-9502-f7122f202dc1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:22:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f840fcc-d3f3-11f1-bc65-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-29T230502Z-1125020976-RC29DOAMMSDH-RTRMADP-3-NORTHKOREA-ARMS.jpg">© KCNA, via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Food safety in India: A challenge for the world's most populous country</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261029-food-safety-in-india-a-challenge-for-the-world-s-most-populous-country</link><description>
India's food industry feeds more than a billion people every day. But ensuring that what reaches consumers is safe has become an increasingly difficult challenge. The country has witnessed a rise in cases of food adulteration, with sometimes fatal consequences. As concerns over adulteration and poor hygiene grow, questions are being raised about whether regulators can effectively oversee such a sprawling sector.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c02c5bc-d39b-11f1-a686-15e3238b6981/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bf7600e4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c02c5bc-d39b-11f1-a686-15e3238b6981/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bf7600e4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2a525e18-d2e7-11f1-87df-79b15ca8b9e2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:15:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Selma DAOUI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hong Kong leader apologises and housing minister resigns after fire investigation exposes failures</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hong-kong-leader-apologises-and-housing-minister-resigns-after-fire-investigation-exposes-failures</link><description>
Hong Kong Chief Executive John Lee apologised on Thursday for a fire that ravaged residential tower blocks in Tai Po in November 2025, killing 168, injuring 79 and displacing thousands of others. Housing Secretary Winnie Ho resigned Wednesday for her department's failure to supervise the maintenance work. A three-month investigation into conduct will follow, alongside proposals to criminalise bid rigging in relation to the complex's US $38 million renovation contract.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b2175bc-d383-11f1-88d2-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4RL864.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b2175bc-d383-11f1-88d2-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4RL864.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">50588f76-d37b-11f1-a962-bb81369cff07</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:29:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b2175bc-d383-11f1-88d2-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4RL864.jpg">© Dale de la Rey, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hello Kitty firm apologises, cuts ties with Japanese spy show after China backlash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hello-kitty-firm-apologises-cuts-ties-with-japanese-spy-show-after-china-backlash</link><description>
Sanrio, the company behind the hugely successful Hello Kitty franchise, has apologised and ended its commercial tie-up with a Japanese TV drama after Chinese state media accused the show of "smearing China", sparking a social media backlash.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c295f5e6-d377-11f1-9e08-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/7271a175a268490239abbd31d47a65dee163760c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c295f5e6-d377-11f1-9e08-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/7271a175a268490239abbd31d47a65dee163760c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c393ea34-d377-11f1-a638-eb58f676ba79</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:04:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c295f5e6-d377-11f1-9e08-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/7271a175a268490239abbd31d47a65dee163760c.jpg">© Pedro Pardo, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>North Korea fires 'around a dozen' ballistic missiles amid rising tensions with South Korea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-north-korea-launches-around-a-dozen-ballistic-missiles-amid-rising-tensions-with-south-korea</link><description>
North Korea fired around a dozen short-range ballistic missiles off its east coast on Thursday, Seoul's defence ministry said. The North Korean capital Pyongyang has stepped up weapons tests in recent weeks despite South Korea's offer of military talks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ac746ca-d365-11f1-9273-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/8efcd0312653794523a7f6070b46e97a42de8d92.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ac746ca-d365-11f1-9273-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/8efcd0312653794523a7f6070b46e97a42de8d92.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d0e96b0-d356-11f1-bb7f-cbaa1567534d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:04:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ac746ca-d365-11f1-9273-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/8efcd0312653794523a7f6070b46e97a42de8d92.jpg">© Philip Fong, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>India: Over 180,000 evacuated on east coast as massive cyclone hits</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-india-over-180-000-evacuated-on-east-coast-as-massive-cyclone-hits</link><description>
A 125-kilometer-per-hour cyclone hit the southeastern coast of India on Wednesday, October 28, as authorities warned of localised flooding and the uprooting of power and communications poles. At least 180,000 people have been evacuated, while neighbouring Sri Lanka and Nepal have also issued weather warnings. Camille Corcoran reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e121a8a-d2bd-11f1-98e6-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-431e2784.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e121a8a-d2bd-11f1-98e6-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-431e2784.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65b986ec-d2bb-11f1-9540-a367598efcc8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:28:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Real Madrid apologises to China over Mbappé's Mao Zedong comments</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261028-real-madrid-apologise-to-china-over-mbapp%C3%A9-s-mao-zedong-comments</link><description>
Real Madrid apologised to the Chinese people on Wednesday after star striker Kylian Mbappé sparked a furious backlash over comments referring to the founding leader of Communist China as a dictator. The club's apology came a day after Mbappé and Spain's La Liga football championship expressed regret over the remarks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3ddc960-d294-11f1-b431-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/fbca039200df0377e79f1baf8b7438362bf844af.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3ddc960-d294-11f1-b431-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/fbca039200df0377e79f1baf8b7438362bf844af.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4a828b8-d294-11f1-a579-6997ff83fa74</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:00:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3ddc960-d294-11f1-b431-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/fbca039200df0377e79f1baf8b7438362bf844af.jpg">© Jade Gao, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>As China's Communist Party holds plenum, Xi's anti-corruption drive continues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues</link><description>
In this edition of Perspective, we try to figure out what happens behind the closed doors of the Chinese Communist Party's plenum meeting. At the heart of the discussions will be President Xi Jinping's firm grip on power. For analysis, we're joined by Jean-François Di Méglio from the Asia Centre think tank.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb005232-d20f-11f1-b098-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-44ed4aec.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb005232-d20f-11f1-b098-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-44ed4aec.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b72c6f3c-d1f6-11f1-bb99-439aefe66b67</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:16:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>Azerbaijan: Rare protests over hijab ban in schools</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools</link><description>
In Azerbaijan, a new government ban on hijab in schools has provoked rare public protests. The ban prohibits clothing deemed "incompatible with the secular principles of general education". While it does not mention Islamic hijab, girls and teachers wearing hijab have been turned away from schools. The measure has sparked tensions in a country where 96% of the population is Muslim.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17098974-d1ef-11f1-89d4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/azerbaidjan-fond-EN.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17098974-d1ef-11f1-89d4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/azerbaidjan-fond-EN.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84e28342-d1ef-11f1-9f38-5b52ec707215</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:16:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Ershad ALIJANI</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Typhoon Champi batters Taiwan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan</link><description>
Typhoon Champi is heading towards China and Japan. Yesterday, it battered Taiwan with heavy rain and winds reaching up to 180 kilometres per hour. Across the island, 56,000 households are without power. Nicolas Chamontin and Ophelie Jacobson report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f59c94bc-cf95-11f1-8d18-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-121303-121445-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f59c94bc-cf95-11f1-8d18-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-121303-121445-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fab3c510-cf95-11f1-b25f-45bbb0637d0b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:33:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Why do women in public life become targets?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets</link><description>
A brutal targeted attack on an Australian female MP, who lost both her legs as a result, has reignited concerns over the rising levels of violence against women in public life. Also Cornell University is facing a no-confidence vote over its handling of an alleged gang rape in 2024. Annette Young speaks to Annie E. Clark, a survivor of campus sexual assault and Dr Sara Wilf of George Mason University about why institutions continue to struggle with sexual assault cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5908bff4-ceeb-11f1-8d64-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-HELEN-HAINES-ATTACK-BEN-BRAHIM-Jennifer.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5908bff4-ceeb-11f1-8d64-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-HELEN-HAINES-ATTACK-BEN-BRAHIM-Jennifer.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b3d0958-cee7-11f1-bf03-a7cbd5a932b9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:58:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Singapore's longevity industry: The quest for eternal youth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth</link><description>
In Singapore, the quest for eternal youth is no longer just a billionaire's fantasy. It's becoming big business. High-tech clinics, longevity labs and specialist companies all promise the same thing: slowing down the ageing process. From continuous metabolic monitoring and genetic testing to supplements and oxygen therapy, every aspect of the body is measured and optimised.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5859209e-ced7-11f1-9bf9-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-63ab9de4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5859209e-ced7-11f1-9bf9-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-63ab9de4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4a9fb60-ce31-11f1-8981-ebbb528b1ec1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:53:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Théo Collet</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Taiwan shuts down schools and businesses as Typhoon Champi approaches</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches</link><description>
As Typhoon Champi approached Taiwan, most businesses and schools were closed across the island Friday and hundreds of flights were canceled in the region. Authorities reported at least one death and dozens of injuries and more than 1,200 people have evacuated their homes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c2df22-ce8d-11f1-90c0-1da646a5f16c/w:1024/p:16x9/d819a05d5c2fe530ae3991168d68541f32c11897.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c2df22-ce8d-11f1-90c0-1da646a5f16c/w:1024/p:16x9/d819a05d5c2fe530ae3991168d68541f32c11897.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6bb5544-ce8d-11f1-a482-a9d16325b13a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:00:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c2df22-ce8d-11f1-90c0-1da646a5f16c/w:1024/p:16x9/d819a05d5c2fe530ae3991168d68541f32c11897.jpg">© I-Hwa Cheng, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Strong earthquake strikes China’s remote Tibet region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven</link><description>
At least 16 people have died and dozens more injured after a major earthquake measuring 7.0 on the Richter scale shook China’s remote Tibet region on Thursday, state media said. Hundreds of houses collapsed in the tremor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9d92e24-ce5b-11f1-9517-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-20T063420Z-1364597011-MT1SPYC0622927-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-PHOTO-LIBRARY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9d92e24-ce5b-11f1-9517-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-20T063420Z-1364597011-MT1SPYC0622927-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-PHOTO-LIBRARY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf26565e-ce5c-11f1-a38e-315ede859882</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:09:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9d92e24-ce5b-11f1-9517-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-20T063420Z-1364597011-MT1SPYC0622927-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-PHOTO-LIBRARY.jpg">© Science Photo Library via Reuter/ Illustration picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Dalai Lama appointed by China 'is going to be a fake one', exiled former Tibetan leader says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, exiled former Tibetan leader Lobsang Sangay said any successor to the Dalai Lama appointed by China "is going to be a fake one". He also likened Beijing's ethnic unity law to "an ethnic erasure", said Tibetan concerns had been "downgraded a bit" in US-China talks and accused China of failing to warn of the deadly August floods on the Nepal-Tibet border.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbc18672-c7b5-11f1-a05b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-Lobsang-Sangay-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbc18672-c7b5-11f1-a05b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-Lobsang-Sangay-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ecb91a8e-c7b4-11f1-bd29-9f686ef585fa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:22:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Down to Earth</category><title>Indonesia continues to battle wildfires, with nearly 2 million hectares burned</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261020-indonesia-continues-to-battle-wildfires-with-nearly-2-million-hectares-burned</link><description>
Fires in Indonesia have burned through more than 1.9 million hectares of land, according to new data, as the country battles its worst wildfire season in a decade. The blazes have sent toxic smoke across much of Southeast Asia, forcing schools to close and fuelling a rise in respiratory illnesses. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7692e870-cbcf-11f1-aae0-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/202610191145AS-ASIA-WEATHERINDONESIA-WILDFIRE-VOLUNTEE-O.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7692e870-cbcf-11f1-aae0-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/202610191145AS-ASIA-WEATHERINDONESIA-WILDFIRE-VOLUNTEE-O.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2fbedfe4-cbd4-11f1-b5e6-1b78e86d5641</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:23:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie DEKIMPE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Driver charged over 'targeted' car attack on Australian lawmaker Helen Haines</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261020-driver-charged-over-targeted-car-attack-on-australian-lawmaker-helen-haines</link><description>
Police on Tuesday charged a driver with intentionally causing serious injury to Australian federal lawmaker Helen Haines, who is in a critical condition after being struck by a car outside her office in an incident that has shocked the nation. Haines had her leg amputated following the attack, according to Australian media reports.
